	"notes": "This is a dashboard app, not a page of prose, so its shell barely changes shape: a thin fixed header on top and a fixed-width icon menu down the left side, both built with flexbox. The only things that ever resize are the search box in the header and the big empty area to the right where a dashboard would draw its charts. On a phone the left menu vanishes and only a hamburger button is left, which this tool never clicked open. Oddly, every screenshot at every width shows that big area completely empty — this looks like an anonymous demo account with no dashboard to show, or a slow-loading list the capture's 1.5-second wait missed, rather than a real layout choice. One scan happened to catch real chart panels rendering, and they are placed by the app's own JavaScript grid system, not by CSS grid or flexbox — a third way to build a layout that neither a screenshot nor the page's stylesheets can show you on their own.",
